From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eriko Kurimoto <elkurin@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:03:33 -0700
Subject: Preserve CacheStorageSideDataWriter across response clones

Previously, CacheStorageSideDataWriter was dropped when a Service
Worker called Response.clone() or cache.put() on a kCacheStorage
Response before passing a clone to FetchEvent.respondWith(), or when
WebRequestProxyingURLLoaderFactory cloned URLResponseHead.

Wrap CacheStorageSideDataWriter in a ref-counted PendingRemote holder
across ResourceResponse and FetchResponseData (replacing SharedRemote
and unifying the pending/bound fields), and consume the PendingRemote
in FetchRespondWithObserver::OnResponseFulfilled() rather than
PopulateFetchAPIResponse() (which is also called by cache.put()).

Also preserve the writer when WebRequestProxyingURLLoaderFactory clones
URLResponseHead before forwarding to OnReceiveResponse().

Bug: 548989584, 570132114, 571209032
Change-Id: I1adaff51c410c3326feedbf551576a20f68defad
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8522482
